# privacy-defaults.patch (Android) -- LW-M7-12 privacy defaults for Fenix:
# strict ETP, HTTPS-Only, delete cookies+cache on quit, no password/card/
# address autofill, DoH off with LibreWolf's provider catalog.
#
# 157 rebase (2026-10-02, Firefox release 157.0): no behaviour change.
#   * Settings.kt, DohSettingsProvider.kt, DeleteBrowsingDataOnQuitFragment.kt,
#     SavedLoginsSettingFragment.kt: upstream reformatted Fenix (ktfmt:
#     `by` on its own line, wrapped KDoc, ASCII-sorted imports), so every
#     hunk was re-applied by hand to the same declarations. The 153 hunks
#     that only moved java.* imports into ASCII order are gone: 157 already
#     sorts them that way.
#   * DohSettingsProvider: the companion object with cloudflareUri/nextDnsUri
#     is still removed (only the test referenced it, and that is updated).
#   * The strict ETP policy in 157 additionally sets fingerprintingProtection;
#     the SettingsTest assertions on it are unchanged and still hold.
#   * Resource XML and the new/updated tests: context offsets only.
